Having stolen a few minutes, a bit closer...

Backtracking, I believe George's error must be coming from=20
openssl/ssl/s3_clnt.c: ssl3_send_client_verify(), the block of code=20
starting 36 lines in, shown below.

There is a call to EVP_SignFinal, that I believe will turn out to=20
dispatch to RSA_sign (openssl/crypto/rsa/rsa_sign.c ).  There is an=20
intermediate maze of twisty passages that abstracts the signature=20
mechanisms, but I'm pretty sure that's where we'll end up.

RSA_sign emits RSA_R_DIGEST_TOO_BIG_FOR_RSA_KEY when the size of the=20
signature generated by i2d_X509_SIG is larger than the size allocated=20
for it in the RSA structure.

Again, this is dependent (indirectly) on TLS version (the check is for=20
md5_sha1 digest, which is used before TLS1.2).
The TLS1.1 path is too well-worn to be likely.  The code (abbreviated)=20
goes like this:

     if(type =3D=3D NID_md5_sha1) {
        ...
         i =3D SSL_SIG_LENGTH;
         s =3D m;
     } else {
            ...
         i=3Di2d_X509_SIG(&sig,NULL);
     }
     j=3DRSA_size(rsa);
     if (i > (j-RSA_PKCS1_PADDING_SIZE))
         {
         RSAerr(RSA_F_RSA_SIGN,RSA_R_DIGEST_TOO_BIG_FOR_RSA_KEY);
         return(0);
         }

This leaves the question of why the RSA structure doesn't have enough space.

Getting further back would be a lot easier with a reproducer and a=20
debugger...

The ssl3_send_client_verify +36:

         if (TLS1_get_version(s) >=3D TLS1_2_VERSION)
             {
             long hdatalen =3D 0;
             void *hdata;
             const EVP_MD *md =3D s->cert->key->digest;
             hdatalen =3D BIO_get_mem_data(s->s3->handshake_buffer,
                                 &hdata);
             if (hdatalen <=3D 0 || !tls12_get_sigandhash(p, pkey, md))
                 {
                 SSLerr(SSL_F_SSL3_SEND_CLIENT_VERIFY,
                         ERR_R_INTERNAL_ERROR);
                 goto err;
                 }
             p +=3D 2;
#ifdef SSL_DEBUG
             fprintf(stderr, "Using TLS 1.2 with client alg %s\n",
                             EVP_MD_name(md));
#endif
             if (!EVP_SignInit_ex(&mctx, md, NULL)
                 || !EVP_SignUpdate(&mctx, hdata, hdatalen)
                 || !EVP_SignFinal(&mctx, p + 2, &u,=20
pkey))                   <=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D breakpoint goes here
                 {
                 SSLerr(SSL_F_SSL3_SEND_CLIENT_VERIFY,
                         ERR_R_EVP_LIB);
                 goto err;
                 }
             s2n(u,p);
             n =3D u + 4;
             if (!ssl3_digest_cached_records(s))
                 goto err;
             }

